<BaseLayout title="Own Your AI Chat Data" description="Why keeping local backups of your AI conversations matters.">
  <h1>Owning Your AI Chat Data</h1>
  <p>TotalRecalls exists because your conversations are yours. Yet most AI platforms make it hard to leave, hard to delete, and hard to export your full history.</p>
  
  <h2>The Problem</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Locked-in exports.</strong> You can export today but rarely search, tag, or migrate.</li>
    <li><strong>Fragile links.</strong> If a provider shuts down or your account is suspended, everything vanishes.</li>
    <li><strong>Vendor lock-in.</strong> Your context, your insights, your research—trapped.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The Solution</h2>
  <p>TotalRecalls moves your conversations onto your hard drive in standard formats (Markdown + JSON). Once local, you control everything:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Search with your own tools.</li>
    <li>Migrate between assistants.</li>
    <li>Back up to any cloud drive.</li>
    <li>Audit your data at any time.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Legal Notes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Exporting conversations is your right under GDPR and CCPA.</li>
    <li>Provider terms (ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Gemini) vary. We never host your tokens.</li>
    <li>TotalRecalls is a local tool; it never sees your credentials.</li>
  </ul>
</BaseLayout>
